VTID-03784 — commands.log
==========================

## Investigation

Read _enterStuckState(), focusGuidedTopic(), _endGuidedTopicTeaching(),
_hide(), and the VTID-03782 circuit-breaker block in _attemptReconnect()
(src/frontend/command-hub/orb-widget.js). Confirmed: the 5-minute
GUIDED_TOPIC_BACKSTOP_MS timer armed in focusGuidedTopic() is only ever
cancelled inside _hide() — no path into the shared _enterStuckState()
(circuit breaker OR MAX_WIDGET_RECONNECTS exhaustion) calls _hide() or
otherwise cancels the backstop.

## Fix applied

Edited src/frontend/command-hub/orb-widget.js:
  _enterStuckState() — added, right after _s._disconnectStuck = true:
    _s._guidedTopicOpenedAt = null;
    try { clearInterval(_s._guidedTopicBackstopInterval); } catch (e) { /* noop */ }
    _s._guidedTopicBackstopInterval = null;
  plus an explanatory comment (see acceptance.md "Fix" section).

  Initially added the same 3 lines only at the VTID-03782 circuit-breaker
  call site in _attemptReconnect() — reconsidered and moved them into the
  shared _enterStuckState() instead, since MAX_WIDGET_RECONNECTS
  exhaustion for a guided-topic session has the exact same latent bug and
  duplicating the fix at one call site would leave the other vulnerable.

$ node --check src/frontend/command-hub/orb-widget.js
SYNTAX_OK

## New test file

Created test/frontend/orb-widget-guided-topic-backstop-stuck-state.test.ts
(5 tests): asserts _enterStuckState() clears _guidedTopicOpenedAt and
cancels the backstop interval, asserts the pre-existing tap-to-reconnect
UI behavior is unchanged, asserts the circuit-breaker call site does NOT
duplicate the cancellation (regression guard for the "fix at one call site
only" mistake caught during development), and asserts MAX_WIDGET_RECONNECTS
exhaustion routes through the same _enterStuckState().

$ npx jest test/frontend/orb-widget-guided-topic-backstop-stuck-state.test.ts
PASS — Test Suites: 1 passed, 1 total / Tests: 5 passed, 5 total

